Before writing or editing any code in this repo, **state the winning condition out loud in your response, verbatim, before doing anything else**:

> **Winning condition: guided, uncertainty-aware capture that provably beats naive photography at finding defects per photo — made real by three things: the `nextBestSurface()` planner (with its uncertainty term), the ghost overlay that makes surface-to-surface comparison honest, and the `/optimize` page that proves the claim numerically instead of asserting it. If a change doesn't strengthen one of those three, it's not the priority right now.**

Then proceed with the task. This isn't decoration — it's a forcing function so a prompt like "can you also add X" doesn't quietly consume the time budget of the three things that actually make this an Optimization-track entry instead of a photo app.

**`SCAN-MASTER-PLAN.md` at the repo root is the current authoritative plan.** Read it before any non-trivial change. `SCAN-EVIDENCE.md` is the live citation/evidence pack for the pitch — every number in it is sourced, don't invent new stats without the same rigor. `SCAN-ARCHITECTURE.md` and `SCAN-TASKS.md` are marked historical inside themselves (they assumed Roboflow-primary; the app is Gemini-primary, confirmed working) — don't build against them. `SCAN-PUNCHLIST.md` tracks bug-fix status.

Hard rules:
- The detector is Gemini-primary with a mock fallback (`src/lib/detect.ts`). Do not start a Roboflow integration — it was evaluated and explicitly deprioritized in `SCAN-PUNCHLIST.md` §0.
- Do not touch LiDAR/ARKit depth APIs — evaluated and rejected (native-only, Pro-iPhone-only, wrong problem for a 2D classification task).
- A real scan must never attach to the seeded sample property (`SAMPLE_PROPERTY_ID` in `store.ts`) — that guard is load-bearing, don't remove it.
- Every external/sponsor API call (Gemini, Auth0, Blob) must degrade gracefully — never let a slow or failed call block the shutter or the identity gate.
- After **12:00 freeze**, nothing new ships. Fix only what's actively broken.
